  "term": "Sleep Disorders, Circadian Rhythm",
  "definition": "Circadian rhythm sleep disorders are sleep problems linked to a disruption of the body’s usual 24-hour sleep–wake pattern. They can occur with travel, shift work, or other causes that disturb normal timing of sleep and waking.",
